<title>NETHERLANDS: ICT over-allotment option exercised.</title>
<headline>ICT over-allotment option exercised.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Merchant bank MeesPierson NV said on Thursday it had exercised the so-called 'green shoe' option to cover over-allotments on shares in Dutch software and services firm ICT Automatisering NV.</p>
<p>This will increase the number of floated shares by 628,721 to 4,820,195. The additional shares were sold by the existing shareholders, MeesPierson said.</p>
<p>ICT was floated in Amsterdam in June at a price of 26 guilders per share. On Thursday, the shares closed at 27.50 guilders, up 0.30 from their previous close.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
